From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan WEGENER <steph.wegener@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:25:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] [Onyx] WebKit2: drop-down lists, the system clipboard,
 downloads by URL, download progress over curl

The pages' <select> lists: WebPopupMenuProxyOnyx hands the items to the embedder through the
view client (WKViewClientV1: showPopupMenu / hidePopupMenu; WKViewSelectPopupMenuItem answers;
an answer after the list closed or was replaced is ignored; a client without the callbacks gets
the list closed at once).

The clipboard: WKSetClipboardCallbacksOnyx gives WebCore's PlatformPasteboard of the UI process
three functions (write the text, read it, the system clipboard's serial); the system's text is
read again when its serial changed, and replaces the in-process content.

WKPageDownloadURLOnyx: a download of a URL for the page (Save Link As...), with the page's
Referer (strict-origin-when-cross-origin) and User-Agent, its cookies; the started callback may
get NULL (the download destroyed before it started).

NetworkDataTaskCurl: a download's didReceiveData now carries the running total and the expected
length (it gave 0, 0: no embedder could show a progress).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
